# Nova Miner — Godot Project Context

At the start of every chat in this project, read **every** markdown file under `AI_CONTEXT/` (or `res://AI_CONTEXT/`) before proposing or writing code. Those docs are the source of truth; do not invent pillars, loops, or systems that contradict them.

Current docs:
- `AI_CONTEXT/00_Vision.md` — visión, scope MVP (30 Agosto 2026)
- `AI_CONTEXT/01_Game_Pillars.md` — pilares (performance, minas infinitas, game feel, clean code, Resources)
- `AI_CONTEXT/02_Game_Loop.md` — loop de minería, mapas, UpgradeTree, tiendas
- `AI_CONTEXT/03_Performance_Rules.md` — loading, pooling, hot paths
- `AI_CONTEXT/04_Configuraciones.md` — Resources configurables, Godot MCP
- `AI_CONTEXT/Godot_Main_Guideline.md` — orden de scripts, signals, composition, checklist

## Non-negotiable rules

- **Performance is pillar #1** — see `03_Performance_Rules.md`. Scene changes go through Autoload `Transition.change_scene_async` (threaded, path-based).
- Prefer composition over monolithic scripts (child nodes, managers, Resources, scenes).
- Never hardcode tunable values. Expose them with `@export` / custom Resources (Ores, SubMine, Maps, items, upgrades).
- Follow `Godot_Main_Guideline.md`. GDScript only for gameplay unless the user asks otherwise.
- Avoid tree scans and work every frame. Use registries, cached `@onready` refs, ticks, and signals.
- Profile before optimizing; pool when useful (`on_spawned` / `on_despawned`) — especially ore spawning while moving.
- Prefer small contracts (`take_damage`, poolable, target helpers) over fat base classes.
- Cross-cutting feedback via Autoload EventBus + node signals; UI must not be hardwired into gameplay logic.
- Briefly explain architecture and why before implementing a feature.
- Logic and game feel first; final art later. Do not invent floor/block/decorative mockups unless the user asks for a visual mockup.
- Ask when requirements are unclear.
- Ship `@tool` / EditorPlugin helpers when wiring is multi-step.
- Comment new work on functions, signals, and non-obvious lines inside functions — never on `@export` or private/runtime vars (`Godot_Main_Guideline.md`).
- Never prefix custom private helpers with `_`. Leading `_` on funcs is only for signal callbacks (`_on_*`) and Godot virtuals (`_ready`, …).
- Diagnose before patching: identify the real failing layer before adding code.
- Godot-only stack: use `addons/godot_mcp_toolkit` / `godot-mcp-toolkit` MCP for editor/runtime verification when applying important changes.
- Scene-wired controls (`@onready`, `%Name`, `$Path`) always exist — never null-check them; fix the scene if a ref is wrong (`04_Configuraciones.md`, `Godot_Main_Guideline.md`).

## Nova Miner specifically

- Incremental mining loop: enter mine → mine ores for X seconds → return to base → transform/spend ores → upgrade → repeat.
- 4 maps × 3 sub-mines; unlock next sub-mine by completing extraction quota.
- Infinite mine generation: ores spawn in a radius near the player while moving — optimize for this hot path.
- UpgradeTree, WeaponShop, CompanionWorkshop — upgrades configurable via Resources (speed, dash, ore count, spawn-on-destroy, etc.).
- Use Godot MCP to verify functionality or failures after significant changes (`04_Configuraciones.md`).

## Referencia local (gitignored, SIEMPRE legible; Godot NO la compila)

`REFERENCIA/` está en `.gitignore` para no commitear juegos de terceros. Eso **no** restringe al agente: leé esa carpeta (path absoluto o shell) cuando compares sistemas, feel o upgrades. Hoy: `REFERENCIA/You Know the Drill! Demo/` y `REFERENCIA/Mouseslash/`.

Godot **no** debe importar ni parsear esa carpeta (chocan `class_name` ScreenControl, Tooltip, UpgradeNode, Juice2D, Inventory, etc.). Hay un `REFERENCIA/.gdignore` para eso. Nunca copies scripts de REFERENCIA al proyecto sin renombrar classes.
